{"title":"Larchwood Bank","sub":"Will AI coding assistants make 2,000 developers 55% faster?","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Banking","geo":"United Kingdom","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"AI productivity · realistic benefit sizing · capacity vs headcount","prompt":"Larchwood Bank employs 2,000 software developers at about $150k a year each, fully loaded. A vendor's study says developers complete tasks 55% faster with its AI coding assistant, which costs $40 per developer a month. The CTO asks what it's really worth, and whether the bank can cancel some of the 150 new hires planned for next year.","clarify":[{"q":"How do developers spend their time?","a":"About 40% writing and changing code; the rest on design, meetings, reviews, testing and support."},{"q":"The vendor's study?","a":"Measured on well-defined coding tasks only."},{"q":"Your own pilot?","a":"Developers who used it regularly spent about 25% less time on coding tasks; about 70% kept using it after a month."},{"q":"Other costs?","a":"About $0.5M for training and security review."}],"structure":{"root":"What is the AI assistant worth to Larchwood?","branches":[{"head":"Time saved","items":["Share of time spent coding","Speed-up on coding","Adoption"]},{"head":"Cost","items":["Licences","Training and security"]},{"head":"Using the time","items":["Fewer hires","More work delivered"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Code quality and security"]}]},"hypothesis":"A 55% speed-up on coding tasks doesn't mean 55% more output, because developers spend most of their time on other things, and not everyone will use the tool.","questions":[{"q":"What would the vendor's claim imply, and what is a realistic estimate?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"391.326719pt\" height=\"202.744pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 391.326719 202.744\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke