oke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_8\"><path d=\"M 38.166719 159.456 L 38.166719 9.768 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_9\"><path d=\"M 38.166719 159.456 L 384.126719 159.456 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(62.903636 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-aa\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(81.109375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(149.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(218.703125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(129.938927 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\" d=\"M 3174 2259 Q 3174 2176 3072 2176 L 480 2170 Q 435 2170 416 2189 Q 397 2208 397 2246 L 397 2522 Q 397 2598 454 2598 L 3110 2598 Q 3174 2598 3174 2534 L 3174 2259 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-aa\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(123.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(183.3125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(252.109375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(200.771094 100.464) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(121.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(190.59375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(271.89451 143.232) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(121.796875 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(340.681677 147.5088) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" d=\"M 2470 4678 Q 2502 4717 2534 4733 Q 2566 4749 2630 4749 L 3059 4749 Q 3136 4749 3136 4672 L 3136 1792 Q 3136 1734 3187 1734 L 3789 1734 Q 3878 1734 3878 1670 L 3878 1357 Q 3878 1274 3789 1274 L 3194 1274 Q 3136 1274 3136 1210 L 3136 96 Q 3136 0 3034 0 L 2598 0 Q 2515 0 2515 83 L 2515 1229 Q 2515 1274 2458 1274 L 384 1274 Q 288 1274 288 1357 L 288 1683 Q 288 1728 313 1776 Q 339 1824 390 1894 L 2470 4678 L 2470 4678 z\nM 2445 1734 Q 2502 1734 2502 1779 L 2502 3910 Q 2502 3987 2483 3993 Q 2464 4000 2413 3936 L 851 1818 Q 787 1734 896 1734 L 2445 1734 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(111.40625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p78ab859132\"><rect x=\"38.166719\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · From headcount to real capacity gained","note":null},"answer":"<p>Read literally, 55% faster across 2,000 developers sounds like 1,100 extra developers of capacity. But it only applies to coding time.</p> <p>Realistic: 2,000 × 40% coding × 25% less time × 70% using it = <b>140 developers' worth</b> of time, about $21M a year.</p> <p>Cost: 2,000 × $480 = $0.96M a year plus $0.5M once. <b>Worth roughly 22× its cost.</b></p>"},{"q":"Can the bank cancel the 150 planned hires?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Not all of them: the realistic gain is about 140 developers' worth, and it is spread across 2,000 people in small slices, not 140 free people.</p> <p>A prudent plan: hire about 80 instead of 150 (bank half the gain), and use the rest to clear the backlog. Review after six months of measured data.</p>"},{"q":"What could go wrong?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Quality:</b> AI-written code can contain bugs or security flaws; keep code review and automated security scanning</li> <li><b>Data:</b> make sure code and customer data don't leave the bank's control</li> <li><b>Measuring:</b> track delivery speed and defect rates, not just how often the tool is used</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Buy the assistant for all developers: it costs about $1.0M a year and is realistically worth about $21M of developer time (140 developers' worth), about 22× its cost. But the vendor's 55% applies only to coding, which is 40% of a developer's time, and not everyone uses the tool. So trim next year's hiring modestly, to about 80 rather than 150, and use the rest to clear the backlog. Keep code review and security scanning in place. Next step: measure delivery speed and defects for six months.","great":["Breaks the vendor's claim into time share × speed-up × adoption","Compares value with cost","Is cautious about turning time saved into fewer hires","Raises quality, security and measurement"],"id":77,"slug":"larchwood-bank"}